 "_doc": "Bears, concept round B1 (2026-10-13): staged here until Dominic picks (D-080: concept-first). Nothing in the game loads this file; tests/sheet.gd and the placement check's cases stage it (CreatureKit.stage). Dominic's direction: bears as a race on two legs, armoured, dignified and intelligent like the Greeks (the smarter counterpart to the rats); rideable on four legs by some races; some bigger still on two legs: polar or old bears, a natural giant line. Built with the creature kit (scenes/art_pixel/creature_kit.gd): three builds of the biped (brown with the shoulder hump and a dished face, black 'moon bear' with big ears, a straight tan muzzle and a pale chest crescent, polar with a long neck and a long roman-nosed head), one quadruped mount, the bronze helmet with ear cups (scenes/art_pixel/bear_concepts.gd). Round B2 (2026-10-13, after Dominic: the giant and its helmet work; the riders' bears have a weird neck and every snout is far too long): every muzzle shortened to a short, broad, blunt one under a rounder skull (the polar's a little longer), the mount carries its own head (mount_head: the biped's, via the kit's head_of, pitched nose-down) low on a short thick neck sloping down from the hump, lifted as it sits (sit.poses.*.head), and an open-faced helmet with the ears out (helm.bear_open). B1's numbers live on as kit variants in tests/sheets/bears_b2.json. Round B3 (2026-10-13, after Dominic: the snouts are perfect, the mounted bear's neck still reads broken; D-126): the mount's neck is one thick mass from the hump into the back of the skull (the kit's neck.into), joined without a line; the polar's neck a little shorter; the open-faced helmet for line soldiers and the ear-cup helmet for giants and elites, each through the ages (helm.bear_open_2, _3, helm.bear_crest_3). B2's numbers live on as kit variants in tests/sheets/bears_b3.json. Since milestone 14 a race needs bonuses: the bears are folk (research faster: the clever ones) with thick fur (+4 hp a unit, priced), placeholders until bears go in play. Sheets and options: docs/concepts/bears/. To put bears in play: move the kits into data/creature_kit.json, the parts into data/parts.json, the creatures, skins and words into their files (DataLib would then complete kit parts), and price them (big hp through points, no special case).",
